  "query_preview": "/Friday through Tuesday/...\nIssued 232 AM MDT TUE AUG 11 2026\nThe active pattern established in the short-term will continue into \nthe long-term period. With southwest flow continuing behind the \nejecting short wave, moisture will continue to overspread our\narea, continuing chances of showers and thunderstorms. High \nterrain near the Nevada border and over the Central Idaho \nMountains will see the highest potential for accumulating \nprecipitation, with a 60-90% chance currently forecast on Friday\nand a 30-60% chance on Saturday. Ridging building back into the\nintermountain west will allow for a drying trend beyond \nSaturday, with isolated afternoon showers/thunderstorms over \nhigher terrain thanks to lingering moisture. Friday into the \nweekend will feature below normal temperatures to start, before \nwarming to near normal come Sunday as the ridge builds in.",
